#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""kk-compare: Swiss basic health insurance (OKP/KVG) premium comparison from the official BAG data.

Ranks every insurer's tariff for one canton/region/age group, works out yearly costs including the
deductible (franchise) and the 10% co-pay, and drafts a cancellation letter. Read-only: it never
contacts an insurer and never sends anything.

  kk-compare [filters] [--franchise 2500] [--model all] [-n 15]     ranked offers
             [--current-insurer X] [--current-premium 512.40] [--current-franchise 2500]
  kk-compare --franchise-matrix [filters] [--model ...]              cheapest offer per franchise and
                                                                     model + break-even vs. CHF 2500
  kk-compare --costs [filters] [--medical 0,500,1000,...]            yearly totals for medical-cost scenarios
  kk-compare --letter [--insurer X] [--policy N] [--out FILE]        cancellation letter draft (prints only)
  kk-compare --region-of PLZ                                         premium region(s) of a postcode
  kk-compare --insurers                                              BAG number -> insurer table
  kk-compare --info | --refresh                                      data provenance / re-download

Filters (defaults: canton, BFS number and place from the assistant profile, region, age and accident from
~/.config/kk/profile.json, which wins): --canton XX --region 1 | --plz 1234 | --bfs 9001, --age adult|young|child,
--accident no|yes. --json prints machine-readable output for the ranking, matrix and costs.

Models: standard (BAG BASE), hmo / hausarzt (BAG PRAXIS, split by tariff name: HMO, "Health
Maintenance", Gesundheitspraxis -> hmo, the rest -> hausarzt), praxis (both), telmed (TEL_DIG),
flex (FLEX: choose between doctor / telmed / pharmacy), pharm (PHARM), managed (all but standard).

Cost model (KVG): yearly total = 12 x premium + min(costs, franchise) + 10% of the rest, co-pay
capped at CHF 700 (children 350). Not included: CHF 15/day hospital contribution, 40% co-pay on
drugs with cheaper generics.

Data (cached in ~/.cache/kk, refreshed after 30 days, --refresh forces it): BAG "Prämien CH" CSV,
"Einzugsgebiete" CSV, "Tarife" CSV (opendata.bagnet.ch, dataset health-insurance-premiums on
opendata.swiss), priminfo praemienregionen-<year>.xlsx. Insurer names and addresses: BAG register
of approved health insurers, October 2026.

Tests: KK_DATA_DIR=<dir> uses fixture files there, KK_OFFLINE=1 never downloads, KK_PROFILE=<file>
another kk profile, ASSISTANT_PROFILE=<file> another owner profile, KK_NOW=<ISO 8601 date or time> pins today
(the letter's default year: this year up to its arrival deadline, then next year; a time without an offset is in
the owner time zone). Tests live in ~/opt/assistant/tests/legacy/kk/run.sh.
"""
import argparse, csv, datetime as dt, hashlib, json, os, re, sys, tempfile, unicodedata
import urllib.request, zipfile
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "lib"))
